    "https://www.lakeforest.edu/academics/majors-and-minors/economics/internships-and-careers": {
      "title": "Internships and Careers",
      "description": "Internships and Careers  | Lake Forest College This website uses cookies so that we can provide you with the best user experience. By using this website, you consent to the use of cookies. Learn more about our use of your data by reading our Privacy Policy. Accept Privacy Policy Apply Visit Campus Request Info Give Students, Faculty, and Staff Search Menu Internships and Careers Academics / Majors and Minors / Economics / Internships and Careers As an economics major at Lake Forest College, you’ll have access to one-on-one career support throughout and after graduation. A wealth of career options opens up with a degree in economics. We’ll help you pick the path that’s best for you. Join our economics graduates in success 100% of Class of 2021 economics majors are pursuing chosen opportunities within 6 months after graduation. 84% of the class of 2021 reported landing a job within six months of graduation, while the other 16 % are continuing their education . Economics Department of Economics, Business, and Finance Faculty Course Descriptions Requirements Student Learning Outcomes Critical Thinking Student Learning Outcomes Student Research Internships and Careers Internship Guidelines Business Finance Contact Information Marie Josephitis Business, Finance, and Data Science Career Pathway Leader mjosephitis@lakeforest.edu 847-735-6102 One Major, Multiple Paths A degree in economics can open up a variety of opportunities. Here's a sample of job titles our newest graduates have held in the last five years: Accountant Actuarial Analyst Assistant Project Manager Associate Consultant Client Coordinator Digital and Social Media Manager Financial Analyst Inside Sales Associate Investment Banking Analyst Marketing Coordinator Recruiter/Talent Coordinator Rotational Credit Analyst Where our graduates land Our students have completed an internship or landed a job with high-profile organizations in and beyond Chicago. Our most recent graduates have interned at or joined the ranks of these companies in the last five years: Allstate CIBC Credit Suisse Ernst and Young Goldman Sachs IBM JPMorgan Chase & Co. Medline Industries Morgan Stanley RBC Wealth Management Walgreens Corporate Wintrust Advancing their studies Economics graduates have also furthered their studies through graduate programs across the country. We set our students up for success so they can enroll in diverse programs such as this sample of degrees pursued by recent graduates: MBA (Kellogg School of Management, Northwestern University; Booth School of Business, University of Chicago) PhD in Economics (Cornell University, University of Wisconsin-Madison, Rice University, University of Illinois Chicago, University of Wyoming, University of Virginia) MA in Public Policy (University of Chicago) Master of Finance (Case Western Reserve University) MS in Data Science (Northwestern University) Juris Doctor (Illinois Institute of Technology-Chicago Kent College of Law; Loyola University School of Law; Northern Illinois University College of Law) A Lake Forest College education is built for the future. All students are equipped with the most sought-after professional skills: writing, speaking, critical thinking, and an understanding of human society and cultures. Our interdisciplinary curriculum sets our graduates apart as competitive and uniquely qualified candidates who are eager to take on the challenges presented in today's professional world. Learn more about how our students turn their passions into a career on our Success Stories and Outcomes page. Success Stories and Outcomes “ I couldn't feel more prepared to start my professional career. Through all my courses, the outstanding professors and faculty, and the great events and opportunities, Lake Forest College has provided me with all the tools to succeed in the future. Natalia Leite '23, Financial Analyst at Goldman Sachs “ As an actuary, risk management is a huge part of my job. The economics major really helped to prepare me for this, especially through lessons on cost/benefit analysis. The small class sizes and personal relationships I was able to form with professors have proven to be very useful in my career. I am more effectively able to communicate ideas to coworkers, and I am better able to work in a team. Rachel Syverud ’23, Pricing Actuary at Allstate These journeys aren't the only way to make it at Lake Forest College. Our career pathways offer a multitude of different ways to take advantage of the education here as well as the opportunities after graduation. Home Our economics graduates... Demonstrate the fundamentals of macroeconomic and microeconomic theories Program and estimate regression equations using sophisticated software Identify and respond to problems with logical analysis and mindfulness of context Test the validity of economic theories using data on a large scale Networking and Career Preparation Learn more about the Forester Network Our students have opportunities to engage with professionals working in various fields of interest and build meaningful connections before graduation. Lake Forest College students don't only get a fantastic education, but also hone applicable skills that employers are seeking in candidates. Our career counselors ensure that our students are well prepared for whatever path they choose. At Lake Forest College, you will have the opportunity to connect with professionals from a multitude of fields. Like what you see? Arrange a campus visit to see what Lake Forest has to offer in person. You'll be able to talk with professors, students, and get a taste for what Lake Forest has to offer your career. Visit Campus Contact the Gorter Family Career Center Pathway Leader Marie Josephitis Business, Finance, and Data Science Career Pathway Leader mjosephitis@lakeforest.edu 847-735-6102 General Contact Gorter Family Career Advancement Center 256 Brown Hall, Middle Campus 847-735-5235 careers@lakeforest.edu Career Pathways Economics majors most often find a home in the Business, Finance, and Data Science Career Pathway, but they can also find a home in any Career Pathway. Business, Finance, and Data Science Law and Public Service Creative Arts and Communication Science and Health Care Build Your Own Career Pathways 555 North Sheridan Road Lake Forest, Illinois 60045 847-234-3100 Admissions: 847-735-5000 Apply Visit Campus Request Information Conference and Event Services Accessibility Services Campus Map College Catalog Consumer Information Emergency Information Non-Discrimination Policy Privacy © 2026 Lake Forest College Accessibility Services Campus Map College Catalog Consumer Information Emergency Information Non-Discrimination Policy Apply Visit Campus Request Info Give About Us Academics Admissions Alumni Athletics Calendar of Events Careers Chicago Community Giving News and Events Offices and Departments Parents Student Life Students, Faculty, and Staff Students, Faculty, and Staff my.lakeforest Quicklinks College Catalog Commencement Faculty & Staff Directory Students, Faculty, and Staff Canvas my.lakeforest my.involvement Webmail Quicklinks Conference and Event Services Job Opportunities Health and Wellness ITS Library Offices and Departments Transcripts, Diplomas, and Verification Letters Web Print About Us Office of the President Administration Mission and Values Our Students Our Alumni Our Campus Conference and Event Services Land Acknowledgement Reputation, Rankings, and Facts Institutional Research Consumer Information Commencement History of the College Public Information and Policies Academics Library Global Engagement Office Majors and Minors Krebs Center for the Humanities Fine Arts Applied Data Center College Catalog Student Honors and Research Academic Resources Summer Classes Dual Credit Classes Admissions Apply First-Year Students Transfer Students International Students Admitted Students Connect With Your Admissions Counselor Visit Campus Forester Flagship Progra