    "https://www.lakeforest.edu/academics/majors-and-minors/entrepreneurship-and-innovation/internships-and-careers": {
      "title": "Internships and Careers",
      "description": "Internships and Careers  | Lake Forest College This website uses cookies so that we can provide you with the best user experience. By using this website, you consent to the use of cookies. Learn more about our use of your data by reading our Privacy Policy. Accept Privacy Policy Apply Visit Campus Request Info Give Students, Faculty, and Staff Search Menu Internships and Careers Academics / Majors and Minors / Entrepreneurship and Innovation / Internships and Careers Join our entrepreneurship graduates in success 96% of Class of 2022 entrepreneurship and innovation minors are pursuing chosen opportunities within 6 months after graduation. 86.4% of the class of 2022 reported landing a job, 9.1% are continuing their education, and 4.5% reported they are engaged in a job search. Entrepreneurship and Innovation Innovation Week Faculty Course Descriptions Requirements Student Learning Outcomes Internships and Careers Entrepreneurship Advisory Council Entrepreneurship Alumni Board Venture Design Challenge News and Events Programs and Opportunities InnovationSpaces Chicago’s Entrepreneurial Ecosystem Oppenheimer Center Contact Information Marie Josephitis Business, Finance, and Data Science Career Pathway Leader mjosephitis@lakeforest.edu 847-735-6102 One Minor, Multiple Paths A minor in entrepreneurship can open up a variety of opportunities. Here's a sample of job titles our newest graduates have held in the last five years: Architectural Design Specialist Assistant Project Manager Automation Business Development Analyst Consumer Experience Digital Project Coordinator Informational Designer Inside Sales Investment Analyst Marketing Associate Patient Access Specialist Product Manager Programs and Engagement Coordinator Where our graduates land Our students have completed an internship or landed a job with high-profile organizations in and beyond Chicago. Our most recent graduates have interned at or joined the ranks of these companies in the last five years: Alight Solutions Aon Best Dedicated Solutions Blue Chip Marketing Worldwide Disney Epic Systems JP Morgan Chase & Co. Kemper Corporation mHUB Northwestern Medicine Oscillas Technologies Walgreens Corporate Advancing their studies Entrepreneurship graduates have also furthered their studies through graduate programs across the country. We set our students up for success so they can enroll in diverse programs such as this sample of degrees pursued by recent graduates: MBA (Loyola University Chicago, DePaul University, Roosevelt University) Master in Business Analytics (University of Southern California) MSW (Indiana University) Master of Finance (Case Western Reserve University) Master of Science in Accountancy (University of Notre Dame) A Lake Forest College education is built for the future. All students are equipped with the most sought-after professional skills: writing, speaking, critical thinking, and an understanding of human society and cultures. Our interdisciplinary curriculum sets our graduates apart as competitive and uniquely qualified candidates who are eager to take on the challenges presented in today's professional world. Learn more about how our students turn their passions into a career on our Success Stories and Outcomes page. Success Stories and Outcomes “ I was looking for a small school near a big city with a solid network. When applying to colleges, I knew I wanted to study Business and Entrepreneurship. The curriculum here was very strong, based on both real life scenarios/skills and theory, which I really appreciated. Hajar Habbal '20, Senior Analyst in Finance Strategy at Kemper Hajar's journey isn't the only way to make it at Lake Forest College. Our career pathways offer a multitude of different ways to take advantage of the education here as well as the opportunities after graduation. Career Pathways Our entrepreneurship graduates... Establish a foundation of confidence to sell themselves and their ideas Cultivate endurance to increase confidence and agency Collaboration and teamwork to help students excel in their future workplaces Grow into leaders by recognizing and nurturing their own strengths in applied settings Networking and Career Preparation Learn more about the Forester Network Our students have opportunities to engage with professionals working in various fields of interest and build meaningful connections before graduation. Lake Forest College students don't only get a fantastic education, but also hone applicable skills that employers are seeking in candidates. Our career counselors ensure that our students are well prepared for whatever path they choose. At Lake Forest College, you will have the opportunity to connect with professionals from a multitude of fields. Like what you see? Arrange a campus visit to see what Lake Forest has to offer in person. You'll be able to talk with professors, students, and get a taste for what Lake Forest has to offer your career. Visit Campus Contact the Gorter Family Career Center Pathway Leaders Marie Josephitis Business, Finance, and Data Science Career Pathway Leader mjosephitis@lakeforest.edu 847-735-6102 Colleen Monks Build Your Own Career Pathway Leader monks@lakeforest.edu 847-735-5237 General Contact Gorter Family Career Advancement Center 256 Brown Hall, Middle Campus 847-735-5235 careers@lakeforest.edu Career Pathways Entrepreneurship minors most often find a home in the Business, Finance, and Data Science Career Pathway, but they can also find a home in any Career Pathway. Business, Finance, and Data Science Law and Public Service Creative Arts and Communication Science and Health Care Build Your Own Career Pathways 555 North Sheridan Road Lake Forest, Illinois 60045 847-234-3100 Admissions: 847-735-5000 Apply Visit Campus Request Information Conference and Event Services Accessibility Services Campus Map College Catalog Consumer Information Emergency Information Non-Discrimination Policy Privacy © 2026 Lake Forest College Accessi