    "https://www.lakeforest.edu/academics/majors-and-minors/environmental-studies/internships-and-careers": {
      "title": "Internships and Careers",
      "description": "Internships and Careers - Environmental Studies  | Lake Forest College This website uses cookies so that we can provide you with the best user experience. By using this website, you consent to the use of cookies. Learn more about our use of your data by reading our Privacy Policy. Accept Privacy Policy Apply Visit Campus Request Info Give Students, Faculty, and Staff Search Menu Internships and Careers Academics / Majors and Minors / Environmental Studies / Internships and Careers Join our Environmental Studies graduates in success! 93% of the class of 2023 reported landing a job within six months of graduation, and 7% planned to continue their education. Environmental Studies Faculty Course Descriptions Requirements Student Learning Outcomes Critical Thinking Student Learning Outcomes Internships and Careers Sustainability Learning in the Field Study Abroad Greenhouse Restoration Contact Information Hilary De Vries Science and Health Care Career Pathway Leader hdevries@lakeforest.edu 847-735-6126 One Major, Multiple Paths A degree in Environmental Studies can open up a variety of opportunities. Here's a sample of job titles our newest graduates have held in the last five years: Conservation and Experiential Programming Aide Communications Assistant Environmental Restoration Specialist Field Ecologist Foster Care Permanency Achievement Specialist Land and Water Steward National Resource Technician Plant Healthcare Technician/Climber Production Specialist Veterinary Technician Where our graduates land Our students have completed an internship or landed a job with high-profile organizations in and beyond Chicago. Our most recent graduates have interned at or joined the ranks of these companies in the last five years: Abbott Laboratories American Conservation Experience Bartlett Tree Experts Burnham Park Animal Hospital Champaign County Forest Preserve District Davey Tree Expert Company Engineering Consulting Services (ECS) Lake Forest Open Lands Olson Ecological Solutions Park Animal Hospital Sustainable Living Guide Tallgrass Restoration LLC Zena Forest Products LLC Advancing their studies Environmental Studies graduates have also furthered their studies through graduate programs across the country. We set our students up for success so they can enroll in diverse programs such as this sample of degrees pursued by recent graduates: Juris Doctor (University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign) Master of Environmental Studies (University of Illinois Springfield) Master of Arts in Leadership (University of Jamestown) Master of Public Health (University of Minnesota) A Lake Forest College education is built for the future. All students are equipped with the most sought-after professional skills: writing, speaking, critical thinking, and an understanding of human society and cultures. Our interdisciplinary curriculum sets our graduates apart as competitive and uniquely qualified candidates who are eager to take on the challenges presented in today's professional world. Learn more about how our students turn their passions into a career on our Success Stories and Outcomes page. Success Stories and Outcomes “ The Environmental Studies department has so many fantastic classes to take, and each of them has the potential to bring out life-changing experiences that can give you clarity on what your true passions are. My experience from my Senior Seminar course on preserving/restoring endangered species gave me an absolute passion to pursue a career related to environmental stewardship and research. Christian Meyers ’23, Land & Water Steward at Green Iowa Americorps Christian's journey isn't the only way to make it at Lake Forest College. Our career pathways offer a multitude of different ways to take advantage of the education here as well as the opportunities after graduation. Career Pathways Our Environmental Studies graduates... Critically Examine all sides of environmental issues and apply understanding from other disciplines Understand the Earth’s Systems on physical, chemical, and biological levels Apply Lessons from various courses through field experiences Actively Challenge existing systems and structures Networking and Career Preparation Learn more about the Forester Network Our students have opportunities to engage with professionals working in various fields of interest and build meaningful connections before graduation. Lake Forest College students don't only get a fantastic education, but also hone applicable skills that employers are seeking in candidates. Our career counselors ensure that our students are well prepared for whatever path they choose. At Lake Forest College, you will have the opportunity to connect with professionals from a multitude of fields. Like what you see? Arrange a campus visit to see what Lake Forest College has to offer in person. You'll be able to talk with professors, students, and get a taste for what Lake Forest College can mean for you and your career. Visit Campus Contact the Gorter Family Career Center Pathway Leader Hilary De Vries Science and Health Care Career Pathway Leader hdevries@lakeforest.edu 847-735-6126 General Contact Gorter Family Career Advancement Center 256 Brown Hall, Middle Campus 847-735-5235 careers@lakeforest.edu Career Pathways Environmental Studies majors most often find a home in the Science and Health Care Pathway, but they can also find a home in any Career Pathway. Business, Finance, and Data Science Law and Public Service Creative Arts and Communication Science and Health Care Build Your Own Career Pathways 555 North Sheridan Road Lake Forest, Illinois 60045 847-234-3100 Admissions: 847-735-5000 Apply Visit Campus Request Information Conference and Event Services Accessibility Services Campus Map College Catalog Consumer Information Emergency Information Non-Discrimination Policy Privacy © 2026 Lake Forest College Accessibility Services Campus Map College Catalog Consumer Information Emergency Information No