    "https://www.lakeforest.edu/academics/majors-and-minors/finance/internships-and-careers": {
      "title": "Internships and Careers",
      "description": "Internships and Careers  | Lake Forest College This website uses cookies so that we can provide you with the best user experience. By using this website, you consent to the use of cookies. Learn more about our use of your data by reading our Privacy Policy. Accept Privacy Policy Apply Visit Campus Request Info Give Students, Faculty, and Staff Search Menu Internships and Careers Academics / Majors and Minors / Finance / Internships and Careers As a finance major at Lake Forest College, you’ll have access to one-on-one career support throughout and after graduation. A wealth of career options opens up with a degree in finance. We’ll help you pick the path that’s best for you. Join our finance graduates in success 100% of Class of 2021 finance m ajors are pursuing chosen opportunities within 6 months after graduation. 9 1% reported landing a job within six months of graduation, while t he other 9 % are continuing their education . Finance Department of Economics, Business, and Finance Faculty Course Descriptions Requirements Student Learning Outcomes Critical Thinking Student Learning Outcomes Student Research Internships and Careers Internship Guidelines Mason School of Business’s Master of Accounting Program Business Economics Contact Information Marie Josephitis Business, Finance, and Data Science Career Pathway Leader mjosephitis@lakeforest.edu 847-735-6102 One Major, Multiple Paths A degree in finance can open up a variety of opportunities. Here's a sample of job titles our newest graduates have held in the last five years: Accounting Specialist Accounts Receivable Analyst Analytic Consultant Executive Compensation Consultant Financial Analyst Financial Development Rotational Program Associate Investment Analyst Management Consultant Quantitative Modeling and Analytics Rotational Analyst Sales and Trading Analyst Treasury Analyst Venture Capital Associate Where our graduates land Our students have completed an internship or landed a job with high-profile organizations in and beyond Chicago. Our most recent graduates have interned at or joined the ranks of these companies in the last five years: Aon Bank of America Merrill Lynch BMO Harris CME Group Ernst and Young Goldman Sachs JPMorgan Chase & Co. Morgan Stanley Morningstar Inc Pepsi Co Pricewaterhouse Coopers Stout Advancing their studies Finance graduates have also furthered their studies through graduate programs across the country. We set our students up for success so they can enroll in diverse programs such as this sample of degrees pursued by recent graduates: MBA (University of Wisconsin-Madison, Loyola University Chicago, UMass Global) Master of Science in Accountancy (College of William and Mary, University of Notre Dame, Loyola University Chicago, DePaul University) Master of Finance (Case Western Reserve University, University of Texas at Dallas) Juris Doctor (University of Iowa, Louisiana State University) A Lake Forest College education is built for the future. All students are equipped with the most sought-after professional skills: writing, speaking, critical thinking, and an understanding of human society and cultures. Our interdisciplinary curriculum sets our graduates apart as competitive and uniquely qualified candidates who are eager to take on the challenges presented in today's professional world. Learn more about how our students turn their passions into a career on our Success Stories and Outcomes page. Success Stories and Outcomes “ Lake Forest prepared me for my career path by the providing a number of resources to assist me in my college journey. Participating in the Loop Program gave me the opportunity to live in the city while interning at BMO, helping me understand how that transition will be after college. Jaronn Correll '23, Corporate Banking Analyst at BMO Capital Markets “ Throughout college, I was lucky to be part of a collaborative and fast paced classroom. The ability to learn in that environment helped me transition into my career. At Stout, we work in teams to complete projects and provide deliverables to clients. Teamwork, presentations, and communication skills, in addition to the ability to think critically, has helped to prepare me to become an active listener and ask questions to my team in the workplace. Jacqueline Rogers ’20, Associate at Stout These journeys aren't the only way to make it at Lake Forest College. Our career pathways offer a multitude of different ways to take advantage of the education here as well as the opportunities after graduation. Career Pathways Our finance graduates... Demonstrate the fundamentals of Microeconomic and Macroeconomic Theory Master core accounting and finance skills Identify and respond to problems with logical analysis and mindfulness of context Form and articulate well-reasoned economic arguments Networking and Career Preparation Learn more about the Forester Network Our students have opportunities to engage with professionals working in various fields of interest and build meaningful connections before graduation. Lake Forest College students don't only get a fantastic education, but also hone applicable skills that employers are seeking in candidates. Our career counselors ensure that our students are well prepared for whatever path they choose. At Lake Forest College, you will have the opportunity to connect with professionals from a multitude of fields. Like what you see? Arrange a campus visit to see what Lake Forest has to offer in person. You'll be able to talk with professors, students, and get a taste for what Lake Forest has to offer your career. Visit Campus Contact the Gorter Family Career Center Pathway Leader Marie Josephitis Business, Finance, and Data Science Career Pathway Leader mjosephitis@lakeforest.edu 847-735-6102 General Contact Gorter Family Career Advancement Center 256 Brown Hall, Middle Campus 847-735-5235 careers@lakeforest.edu Career Pathways Finance majors most often find a home in the Business, Finance, and Data Science Pathway, but they can also find a home in any Career Pathway. Business, Finance, and Data Science Law and Public Service Creative Arts and Communication Science and Health Care Build Your Own Career Pathways 555 North Sheridan Road Lake Forest, Illinois 60045 847-234-3100 Admissions: 847-735-5000 Apply Visit Campus Request Information Conference and Event Services Accessibility Services Campus Map College Catalog Consumer Information Emergency Information Non-Discrimination Policy Privacy © 2026 Lake Forest College Accessibility Services Campus Map College Catalog Consumer Information Emergency Information Non-Discrimination Policy Apply Visit Campus Request Info Give About Us Academics Admissions Alumni Athletics Calendar of Events Careers Chicago Community Giving News and Events Offices and Departments Parents Student Life Students, Faculty, and Staff Students, Faculty, and Staff my.lakeforest Quicklinks College Catalog Commencement Faculty & Staff Directory Students, Faculty, and Staff Canvas my.lakeforest my.involvement Webmail Quicklinks Conference and Event Services Job Opportunities Health and Wellness ITS Library Offices and Departments Transcripts, Diplomas, and Verification Letters Web Print About Us Office of the President Administration Mission and Values Our Students Our Alumni Our Campus Conference and Event Services Land Acknowledgement Reputation, Rankings, and Facts Institutional Research Consumer Information Commencement History of the College Public Information and Policies Academics Library Global Engagement Office Majors and Minors Krebs Center for the Humanities Fine Arts Applied Data Center College Catalog Student Honors and Research Academic Resources Summer Classes Dual Credit Classes Admissions Apply First-Year Students Transfer Students International Students Admitted Students Connect With Your Admissions Counselor Visit Campus Forester Flagship Program Scholarships Financial Aid High School Counselors Community C