    "https://www.lakeforest.edu/academics/majors-and-minors/nursing-pathways-program/internships-and-careers": {
      "title": "Internships and Careers",
      "description": "Internships and Careers - Nursing Pathways Program  | Lake Forest College This website uses cookies so that we can provide you with the best user experience. By using this website, you consent to the use of cookies. Learn more about our use of your data by reading our Privacy Policy. Accept Privacy Policy Apply Visit Campus Request Info Give Students, Faculty, and Staff Search Menu Internships and Careers Academics / Majors and Minors / Nursing Pathways Program / Internships and Careers Nursing Pathways students are encouraged to take advantage of an impressive array of internship opportunities across the Chicagoland area which will allow them to gain early first-hand experience in the field.  Some sites that commonly host our interns are: North Shore University Health System Northwestern Medicine - Lake Forest Hospital Rush University Medical Center Lurie Children's Hospital Shirley Ryan AbilityLab Nursing Pathways Program Requirements Rosalind Franklin University Flexible Nursing Pathways Student Learning Outcomes Internships and Careers Program Committee Contact Information Ann Maine, PhD Assistant Professor of Biology Director, Pre-Health Advising Director, Health Professions Program and Nursing Pathways Program Lillard Science Center 246 847-735-6037 maine@lakeforest.edu Khadija Manzoor Career Advising Contact Career Advancement Center kmanzoor@lakeforest.edu “ I've thought about becoming a nurse in the emergency room. That's always appealed to me. But during my internship, I've seen a variety of places such as case management and the operating room, the PACU, which is the post-anesthesia care unit, and the UCC, the Universal Care Center, which is where patients go before surgery. So this has really opened up a lot of doors for me about what I may be interested in in the future. Ben Reynaldo '22 Hometown: Chicago, IL Summer internship: A first glimpse into the nursing field A partnership between Lake Forest College and Lake Forest Hospital gives students who are interested in nursing careers an opportunity to spend a day in a nurse’ s shoes. Through this summer internship, students shadow professionals, g aining a real- time , in-person glimpse into healthcare fields . The immersive experience develops the students’ understanding of the complex ity of healthcare environments while also showcasing the diversity in careers available for nurses . Read More Your Career Advisor Will Have Your Back Starting From Day One Our unique Career Pathways preparation program takes students through four stages of personal exploration and career development we call the Career Milestones. We help students gain the skills and experiences they need to be successful and to build a strong network within their Pathway, a network that will provide them with industry insight and help them land meaningful jobs.  Nursing Pathways Program participants most often find a home in the Science and Health Care Career Pathway , but they can also find a home in any Career Pathway. Lake Forest College alumni have gone on to obtain rewarding careers in the nursing field around the country. Foresters have landed jobs at prestigious hospitals and health care networks including: Rush University Medical Center North Shore Health Systems University of Iowa Hospitals and Clinics University of Chicago Humana Healthcare Northwestern Medicine St. Louis Children's Hospital Loyola Medicine Mayo Clinic Lucile Packard Children's Hospital Stanford Ann & Robert H. Lurie Children's Hospital of Chicago 555 North Sheridan Road Lake Forest, Illinois 60045 847-234-3100 Admissions: 847-735-5000 Apply Visit Campus Request Information Conference and Event Services Accessibility Services Campus Map College Catalog Consumer Information Emergency Information Non-Discrimination Policy Privacy © 2026 Lake Forest College Accessibility Services Campus Map College Catalog Consumer Information Emergency Information Non-Discrimination Policy Apply Visit Campus Request I