    "https://www.lakeforest.edu/academics/majors-and-minors/sociology-and-anthropology/internships-and-careers": {
      "title": "Internships and Careers",
      "description": "Internships and Careers - Sociology and Anthropology  | Lake Forest College This website uses cookies so that we can provide you with the best user experience. By using this website, you consent to the use of cookies. Learn more about our use of your data by reading our Privacy Policy. Accept Privacy Policy Apply Visit Campus Request Info Give Students, Faculty, and Staff Search Menu Internships and Careers Academics / Majors and Minors / Sociology and Anthropology / Internships and Careers Join our sociology and anthropology graduates in success 100% of the class of 2023 reported landing a job or enrolling in graduate school within six months of graduation. Sociology and Anthropology Faculty Course Descriptions Requirements Student Learning Outcomes Critical Thinking Student Learning Outcomes Internships and Careers Resources Contact Information Deja McClellan Law and Public Service Career Pathway Leader dmcclellan@lakeforest.edu 847-735-6233 One Major, Multiple Paths A degree in Sociology and Anthropology can open up a variety of opportunities. Here's a sample of job titles our newest graduates have held in the last five years: Applied Behavioral Analysis Clinical Associate Behavioral Therapist Correctional Officer Design Researcher Admissions Counselor Interpretive Naturalist Project Manager Protective Services Caseworker Student Needs Facilitator Teacher Where our graduates land Our students have completed an internship or landed a job with high-profile organizations in and beyond Chicago. Our most recent graduates have interned at or joined the ranks of these companies in the last five years: AbbVie Aon Autism Home Support Services CDW Conifer Research Dunes Learning Center James R. Jordan Foundation Northwestern University PEAK6 WorldChicago Advancing their studies Sociology and Anthropology graduates have also furthered their studies through graduate programs across the country. We set our students up for success so they can enroll in diverse programs such as this sample of degrees pursued by recent graduates: Juris Doctor (Georgetown University Law Center) Master of Arts in International Studies (University of San Francisco) Masters of Science in Education in Adult and Higher Education (Northern Illinois University) Master of Science, Library and Information Science (University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign) Master of Social Work (Loyola University Chicago) A Lake Forest College education is built for the future. All students are equipped with the most sought-after professional skills: writing, speaking, critical thinking, and an understanding of human society and cultures. Our interdisciplinary curriculum sets our graduates apart as competitive and uniquely qualified candidates who are eager to take on the challenges presented in today's professional world. Learn more about how our students turn their passions into a career on our Success Stories and Outcomes page. Success Stories and Outcomes “ Being involved in as many leadership opportunities as I could while attending Lake Forest College not only allowed me to grow individually, but also professionally. I have learned the importance of having confidence in your ideas, while also trusting others in working as a team. Samantha Dolatowski '22, Kit Development Coordinator at Hand2Mind Samantha's journey isn't the only way to make it at Lake Forest College. Our career pathways offer a multitude of different ways to take advantage of the education here as well as the opportunities after graduation. Career Pathways Our Sociology and Anthropology graduates... Design and execute a research project on social phenomena involving human subjects Apply sociological and anthropological insights and principles Understand core ideas: sociological imagination and cultural relativism Actively challenge existing systems, structures, and policies of racism and inequality Networking and Career Preparation Learn more about the Forester Network Our students have opportunities to engage with professionals working in various fields of interest and build meaningful connections before graduation. Lake Forest College students don't only get a fantastic education, but also hone applicable skills that employers are seeking in candidates. Our career counselors ensure that our students are well prepared for whatever path they choose. At Lake Forest College, you will have the opportunity to connect with professionals from a multitude of fields. Like what you see? Arrange a campus visit to see what Lake Forest has to offer in person. You'll be able to talk with professors, students, and get a taste for what Lake Forest has to offer your career. Visit Campus Contact the Gorter Family Career Center Pathway Leader Deja McClellan Law and Public Service Career Pathway Leader dmcclellan@lakeforest.edu 847-735-6233 General Contact Gorter Family Career Advancement Center 256 Brown Hall, Middle Campus 847-735-5235 careers@lakeforest.edu Career Pathways Sociology and Anthropology majors most often find a home in the Law and Public Service Career Pathway, but they can also find a home in any Career Pathway. Business, Finance, and Data Science Law and Public Service Creative Arts and Communication Science and Health Care Build Your Own Career Pathways 555 North Sheridan Road Lake Forest, Illinois 60045 847-234-3100 Admissions: 847-735-5000 Apply Visit Campus Request Information Conference and Event Services Accessibility Services Campus Map College Catalog Consumer Information Emergency Information Non-Discrimination Policy Privacy © 2026 Lake Forest College Accessibility Services Campus Map College Catalog Consumer Information Emergency Information Non-Discrimination Policy Apply Visit Campus Request Info Give About Us Academics Admissions Alumni Athletics Calendar of Events Careers Chicago Community Giving News and Events Offices and Departments Parents Student Life Students, Faculty, and Staff Students, Faculty, and Staff my.lakeforest Quicklin