    "https://www.lakeforest.edu/careers/getting-started/forester-career-closet": {
      "title": "Forester Career Closet",
      "description": "Forester Career Closet  | Lake Forest College This website uses cookies so that we can provide you with the best user experience. By using this website, you consent to the use of cookies. Learn more about our use of your data by reading our Privacy Policy. Accept Privacy Policy Apply Visit Campus Request Info Give Students, Faculty, and Staff Search Menu Forester Career Closet Careers / Getting Started / Forester Career Closet The Forester Career Closet is an on-campus resource that provides free professional clothing to students. The Career Closet is located in the basement in Deerpath Hall . Operated by the Gorter Family Career Advancement Center and made possible by generous clothing donations from the Forester community, this campus resource helps students to dress their best for interviews, networking events, internships and other professional activities. Find your next professional outfit—for free! Build your professional wardrobe from our selection of shirts, dresses, skirts, blazers, suits, sweaters, trousers, shoes, and accessories. We carry a range of fits, styles, and colors in a variety of sizes. Students may take (and keep!) a total of five items per semester. The \"Casual Closet\" inside the Career Closet offers a select section of casual clothing. Winter coats and other winter gear is available thanks to a special initiative by Residence Life. Take a professional headshot photo. Use our Career Closet photo station to get a photo taken for your LinkedIn and Handshake profile. We provide a solid colored background and photo lighting, and we will take your photo on your phone to allow for easy upload access to your online profiles. Visit the Closet Drop-In Hours: Drop in hours will be updated at the beginning of each semester . Please try to limit your visit to 30-45 minutes so that we can accommodate as many students as possible. Appointments: If you are unable to come to the Career Closet drop-in hours, please email careers@lakeforest.edu to make a 30-minute appointment. Offer 2-3 times you are available, and please schedule your appointment at least one week in advance. Donate to the Closet Make a difference by cleaning out your closet! Clothing donations from our community keep the Closet running and provide students with an essential resource as they prepare for interviews, internships, and more. Drop-Off: Clothing donations can be dropped off at the CAC Main Office, Brown Hall 256 Monday-Friday from 8:30a.m.-5p.m. Let us know if you would like a tax receipt when you drop off. Mailing Donations: Please mail donations to: Gorter Family Career Advancement Center 256 Brown Hall, Middle Campus Lake Forest College 555 N. Sheridan Road Lake Forest, IL 60045 Items Accepted: New or gently-used business casual and business professional clothing. We are always in need of: Women’s size blouses, suits, and separates (especially XS/S, and plus-sized or XXL) Men’s size small suits and sport coats and Men’s size 6-12 shoes Padfolios, work bags, and briefcases Scrubs (all sizes) Winter coats and other winter gear can be donated at Van Ness House through our Office of Residence Life. Career Connections Career Pathways Internships The Forester Network Recruiting Resources for Employers Getting Started GO Networking Career Resources Career Express Advising Forester Career Closet Success Stories and Outcomes Meet Our Staff Contact Information Gorter Family Career Advancement Center 256 Brown Hall, Middle Campus 847-735-5235 careers@lakeforest.edu Hours Academic Year: Monday–Friday, 8:30 a.m. to 5 p.m. Follow Us! 555 North Sheridan Road Lake Forest, Illinois 60045 847-234-3100 Admissions: 847-735-5000 Apply Visit Campus Request Information Conference and Event Services Accessibility Services Campus Map College Catalog Consumer Information Emergency Information Non-Discrimination Policy Privacy © 2026 Lake Forest College Accessibility Services Campus Map College Catalog Consumer Information Emergency Informati